{{- /* internal/render/templates/suggestion.gohtml — one comment's
suggestions as a row of cards (§7.4): CSS grid
(grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr))), bead .5's
rule to write against the "suggestions" class below. Within one card, pros
and cons sit in their own two-column sub-grid as sibling containers — never
one nested inside the other — so a reader's eye moves left-right between
"why" and "what it costs". effort and scope, both structurally-constrained
enums, render as small badges in the card header, not prose. A
suggestion's own code excerpt, when present, sits at the bottom of its
card, through the same {{template "code"}} partial (bead .4) every other
excerpt uses — omitted entirely, not emitted empty, when the suggestion
carries none (§12). Dot is []htmlSuggestionView
(internal/render/html_view_finding.go). */ -}}
{{define "suggestion"}}
<div class="suggestions">
{{range .}}
<div class="suggestion-card">
<div class="suggestion-header">
<span class="suggestion-summary">{{.Summary}}</span>
<span class="tag tag-effort">{{.Effort}}</span>
<span class="tag tag-scope">{{.Scope}}</span>
</div>
<div class="suggestion-pros-cons">
<div class="suggestion-pros">
<h4>Pros</h4>
<ul>{{range .Pros}}<li>{{.}}</li>{{end}}</ul>
</div>
<div class="suggestion-cons">
<h4>Cons</h4>
<ul>{{range .Cons}}<li>{{.}}</li>{{end}}</ul>
</div>
</div>
{{if .HasCode}}{{template "code" .Code}}{{end}}
</div>
{{end}}
</div>
{{end}}
